diagnosis_text:
A full diagnostic sweep of the dc_clos_bgp topology finds no fault — current or residual — consistent with the reported overnight outage.

**Affected component:** None identified. All subsystems are healthy.

**Mechanism (why the lab is clean):** The topology provides a fully redundant Clos fabric: each leaf router (leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1) holds two BGP sessions — one to spine_router_0_0 and one to spine_router_0_1 — and both spines peer with super_spine_router_0. All five routers show FRR daemons active (watchfrr, zebra, bgpd), all BGP sessions Established, and the correct host prefixes (10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24) advertised. Even if a single inter-switch link had failed and recovered, BGP would have reconverged over the surviving path within seconds, leaving a BGP session disruption trace. No such trace exists.

**Localization:** No device is implicated. infra_sweep found zero flagged devices across all seven nodes; l2_snapshot confirmed no duplicate MACs and no down or missing interfaces; tc_snapshot found no traffic shaping on any of the 16 inspected interfaces; pressure_sweep found no flap scripts, stress tools, or resource pressure on any device.

**Root cause:** The reported pc_0_0 → pc_0_1 outage leaves no detectable mechanism or historical trace in the live lab — no link-down history, no BGP session disruption, no ACL rule, no carrier-change anomaly — and current end-to-end reachability is 0% loss in both directions.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. The fabric is operating normally. If the outage recurs, capture `show bgp summary` and interface carrier counters at the time of failure for a definitive diagnosis.
=== END ===